.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt CEDRUS 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cedrus
.Nd Allwinner A64 video engine, stateless MPEG-2 and H.264 decoder
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the module at boot time, place the following lines in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dmabuf_base_load="YES"
media_load="YES"
cedrus_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver controls the video engine of the Allwinner A64 (Banana Pi M64, Pine64, and others) and
exposes it as a stateless V4L2 decoder, as defined by the Linux
.Dq stateless decoder
interface.
It attaches to
.Xr simplebus 4
to the device tree node compatible with
.Dq allwinner,sun50i-a64-video-engine
that has one register window, the clocks
.Dq ahb ,
.Dq mod
and
.Dq ram ,
and one reset line.
Each attach creates one
.Pa /dev/videoN
and one
.Pa /dev/mediaN
.Pq see Xr media 4 .
.Pp
The module depends on
.Xr media 4 ,
which depends on
.Xr dmabuf 4
.Pq Sy dmabuf_base .
.Pp
The interface a program has to use, the supported formats and controls and the conventions that
differ between decoders are in
.Xr v4l2_stateless 7 .
In short, the OUTPUT queue takes
.Dv V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264_SLICE
or
.Dv V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG2_SLICE ,
the CAPTURE queue returns NV12, and the picture parameters are controls set in a media request.
The engine writes the capture buffers directly; they can be exported with
.Dv VIDIOC_EXPBUF
and imported by a GPU or display driver without a copy.
.Pp
Capabilities:
MPEG-2 I, P and B pictures, frame and field structure, 4:2:0;
H.264 8-bit 4:2:0 and 8-bit monochrome streams, frame pictures, field pictures
and MBAFF, I, P and B slices, multiple slices and reference frames, long-term references,
explicit weighted prediction, scaling lists.
Not supported by the hardware as measured, or not implemented: bit depths above 8, 4:2:2 and 4:4:4,
slice groups (FMO), SP and SI slices, and separate colour planes.
Such streams are refused with the buffers flagged with an error.
Frame sizes are 16 to 2048 pixels in each dimension.
.Pp
The engine reaches only part of DRAM (addresses relative to the DRAM base): the driver allocates
all buffers as contiguous memory inside that window.
Large pictures need large contiguous blocks; see
.Sx BUGS .
.Sh LOADER TUNABLES
These are read with
.Xr kenv 1
when the driver attaches; set them in
.Xr loader.conf 5 .
.Bl -tag -width ".Va hw.cedrus.lab_lo_mb"
.It Va hw.cedrus.pm
Power management.
The default is 1: the engine's clocks are gated about 200 ms after its last use.
0 keeps it powered.
.It Va hw.cedrus.lab
If 1, creates
.Pa /dev/cedrus-lab
(owner root, group wheel, mode 0600), a register laboratory used for the measurements the driver is
built from, and allocates
.Va hw.cedrus.lab_size
bytes of contiguous memory for it.
Disables power management.
The default is 0.
For developers only.
.It Va hw.cedrus.lab_size
Size of the laboratory buffer in bytes.
The default is 8388608 (8 MiB).
.It Va hw.cedrus.lab_lo_mb
If not 0, the lowest address, in MiB from the DRAM base, at which the laboratory buffer may be
placed.
The default is 0.
.El
.Pp
A reserved pool of contiguous memory for the decoder buffers (planned as
.Va hw.cedrus.pool_mb )
is not in the driver yet and is not read.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following variables are under
.Va dev.cedrus.0 .
.Pp
Statistics (read-only):
.Bl -tag -width ".Va h264_hdrmode"
.It Va pictures
Pictures decoded.
.It Va errors
Pictures that ended in an error.
.It Va timeouts
Pictures that timed out.
.It Va rejects
Pictures rejected before they reached the engine.
.It Va missing_refs
Reference pictures that were not found.
.It Va skip_busy
Skip commands that found the bit stream reader busy.
.It Va h264_last
The buffer addresses of the last H.264 slice (string).
.El
.Pp
Writable:
.Bl -tag -width ".Va h264_hdrmode"
.It Va h264_hdrmode
Convention of the
.Va header_bit_size
field of the H.264 slice parameters.
1 (the default): the bits from the NAL header byte to the start of slice data, counted in the RBSP
(no start code, no emulation prevention bytes), as FFmpeg gives them.
0: counted from the start code.
See
.Xr v4l2_stateless 7 .
.It Va dma_mb
How many MiB of DRAM, from the DRAM base, the capture buffers and the engine's buffers may use.
The default is 1024.
Takes effect when a device is opened.
.It Va src_mb
The same limit for the OUTPUT (stream) buffers.
The default is 1024.
.It Va aux_mb
MiB from the DRAM base for the engine's own buffers.
The default is 64.
.It Va mv_kb
If not 0, forces the size of the per-picture motion vector buffer in KiB.
The default is 0 (computed).
For experiments.
.It Va scratch_kb
If not 0, forces the size of the scratch buffer in KiB.
The default is 0 (computed).
For experiments.
.It Va aux_near
If not 0, takes the engine's buffers from the picture's 64 MiB segment.
The default is 0.
For experiments.
.It Va h264_oldskip
If not 0, waits for a status bit that is always set after a skip, as the first versions did.
The default is 0.
For experiments.
.It Va mod_mhz
If not 0, asks the clock framework for this engine clock rate in MHz.
The default is 0 (leave it).
For experiments; a clock above nominal does not make the engine faster.
.It Va h264_trace
Writing 1 prints the register writes of the last H.264 slice to the console.
.It Va dump
Writing 1 prints the first registers of the engine.
.It Va sram_claim
Sets or clears the SRAM C1 mapping bit.
.It Va sram0
Writes the system-control register 0.
.It Va poke_addr , Va poke , Va peek
Write a word at, or print the word at, the physical address in
.Va poke_addr .
.El
.Pp
.Va dump ,
.Va sram_claim ,
.Va sram0 ,
.Va poke_addr ,
.Va poke
and
.Va peek
touch hardware registers and arbitrary physical memory: they exist for the measurements and can
crash the system.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /dev/cedrus-lab"
.It Pa /dev/videoN
The decoder.
.It Pa /dev/mediaN
Its media controller device.
.It Pa /dev/cedrus-lab
The register laboratory (only with
.Va hw.cedrus.lab Ns =1 ) .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr media 4 ,
.Xr dmabuf 4 ,
.Xr v4l2_stateless 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver is part of the freebsd-media project, 2026.
Its register programming was found by measuring an unmodified engine; the measurements are in
.Pa docs/cedrus-facts .
.Sh BUGS
A 1080p picture needs 3 MB contiguous OUTPUT buffers and contiguous capture buffers.
After a long uptime, or with the GPU stack loaded, physical memory is fragmented and
.Dv VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS
or
.Dv VIDIOC_REQBUFS
fail with
.Er ENOMEM .
Load the modules from the loader, or reboot.
.Pp
MPEG-2 output is within two sample values of a software decoder: the inverse transform is not
bit-exact.
